cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use noWorkflow in your research, please cite it as below.
  Each release is a tag of this repository; cite the one you used.
title: noWorkflow
type: software
abstract: >-
  noWorkflow traces the provenance of Python scripts without changes to
  the script: what the script defined, executed, read and wrote, the
  processes it launched and the programs they ran, stored in a local
  database that can be queried, compared between trials, restored and
  exported.
